
- The reference file is ALWAYS the png

- The png file can be any size (<=256px)

- The name of the file MUST represente its content and NOT how it will be used !
For example, the oriented circle must be named "circle-clockwise..." and NOT "rotate..."

- The filename can be what you want but it MUST contain the hotspot of the cursor
(hotspot: the pixel in the image which will correspond to the pixel clicked on the screen)
The formatting of the hotspot MUST BE: .<HotspotX>x<HotspotY>
The hotspot must be between [0,100], "0%x0%" = top-left corner, "50%x50%" = center, "100%x100%" = bottom-right corner

- Each time a png is updated, run (on linux-like (WSL,mac,...) with icoutils package installed):
    python3 ./build.cur.py

---

- When ADDING a new png cursor file:
    - run the script
    - update the code:
        ...\IliadEditor\OdysseyPainterEditor\Public\Tools\OdysseyPainterEditorTool.h
        - add a new entry in EMouseCursorCustom enum
        ...\IliadEditor\OdysseyPainterEditor\Public\Tools\OdysseyPainterEditorTool.cpp
        - add new corresponding id <-> file entry at the end of FMouseCursor::InitializeCustomCursorMap()
        - use the cursor id everywhere it's needed

- When only UPDATING a png cursor file:
    - run the script
